          "case_name": "In re Interest of DeWayne G., Jr.",
          "citation": "263 Neb. 43, 638 N.W.2d 510 (2002)",
          "court": "Nebraska Supreme Court",
          "year": 2002,
          "date_decided": "2002-01-25",
          "holding": "The court held that Neb. Rev. Stat. § 43-283.01 gives a parent no right to demand a separate pre-termination hearing on whether reasonable efforts to preserve and reunify the family were made, and reinstated the termination of parental rights.",
          "relevance": "The statute the court construes directs that reasonable efforts be made to prevent the need for removal, which is the mandate behind voluntary service plans.",
          "quote": "the plain language of § 43-283.01 contains no such directive granting a parent or any other party the right to bring a motion requesting a \"separate hearing\"",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/1810106/in-re-dewayne-g-jr/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 1810106
        },
        {
          "case_name": "In re Interest of Carmelo G.",
          "citation": "296 Neb. 805, 896 N.W.2d 902 (2017)",
          "court": "Nebraska Supreme Court",
          "year": 2017,
          "date_decided": "2017-06-02",
          "holding": "The court held that a delay of more than eight months between entry of an ex parte temporary custody order and the protective custody order was unreasonable and violated the mother's procedural due process rights.",
          "relevance": "Safety plans with voluntary services are described as the tool used when services can keep the child at home.",
          "quote": "due process rights include the right to be free from an unreasonable delay in providing a parent a meaningful hearing after the entry of an ex parte temporary custody order",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4421961/in-re-interest-of-carmelo-g/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 4421961
        }
